From 941fb27950acca0a0826930efe5caaccb20f47c0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: soulexit <metehan.tanriverdi01@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 12:06:17 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 56/56] panvk: v7 ARMSX2 (PCSX2) support, overlap barriers, UBO
 push

Kingdom Hearts in ARMSX2 on the G76 (Kirin 990): 5-8 FPS -> 27-30.

- EXT/ARM_rasterization_order_attachment_access on v6/v7: PCSX2 reads
  the render target with fbfetch instead of recording a feedback-loop
  barrier per draw that split every pass (~860 splits/s). Forward pixel
  kill off and depth/stencil tile reads ordered when a draw uses it.
  CTS rasterization_order_attachment_access: 122 pass, 0 fail.
- Tile-local barriers inside a render pass (BY_REGION, attachment output
  to fragment-shader reads) no longer split the pass
  (PANVK_SPLIT_TILE_BARRIERS=1 restores the split).
- Vertex/tiler work of a batch overlapping the previous fragment job is
  on by default, with split tiler heap halves of 128 MiB. A barrier from
  fragment-side work to vertex input, pre-rasterization, compute or
  transfer stages makes the next batch wait for the fragment job
  (after_frag): synchronization CTS writes read by the tessellation and
  geometry emulation. PANVK_OVERLAP=0 turns overlap off.
- Dynamic uniform buffer words that vertex and fragment shaders read at
  constant offsets go to the push uniforms (FAU), read from the buffer's
  memory when the draw is recorded: on by default for PCSX2-based
  emulators only (PANVK_V7_PUSH_UBO=1/0). -12% GPU time on the large
  passes. panvk_device_memory_cpu_ptr() maps memory the application has
  not mapped.
- Direct texture/sampler indexing for ordinary bindings
  (PANVK_V7_DIRECT_TEX_ALL=1, off by default): shaders reading a push
  descriptor set keep their per-draw tables (vk_meta blits lost the
  device).
- Direct indexed draws can find their index range on the CPU and be
  recorded as direct draws (PANVK_V7_CPU_INDEX_RANGE=1, off by default:
  indices written after recording would give a stale range).
- panvk_env.txt is read with open()+fdopen(): AdrenoTools (ARMSX2) hooks
  fopen() into the driver cache directory. PANVK_STDERR_FILE uses dup2().
- Diagnostics: PANVK_GPU_TS=1 GPU timestamps of vertex/tiler chains in
  the GPU profile, CPU wait sites by caller, the sampling profiler per
  thread and symbol, image creation log (PANVK_LOG_IMAGES), in-pass
  barrier log (PANVK_LOG_PASS_BARRIERS), batch reasons.

CTS (release build): no new failures against 1.2.4 on the regression
sample (18 846 pass), tile barriers, rasterization order, vertex-shader
images, 6 890 indirect draws, buffer-to-image copies, descriptor
indexing, mutable descriptors and sync2; UBO cases 375/375 with UBO push
forced on.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
